---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — OpenCoven';
const description = "OpenCoven Privacy Policy. Learn what data OpenCoven collects, how it's used, and how we keep your information private.";
const sections = [['who-we-are','Who We Are'],['what-we-dont-collect',"What We Don't Collect"],['what-we-do-collect','What We Do Collect'],['cookies','Cookies and Analytics'],['third-party','Third-Party Services'],['how-we-use','How We Use Your Data'],['storage','Data Storage and Security'],['your-rights','Your Rights'],['children',"Children's Privacy"],['changes','Changes to This Policy'],['contact','Contact']];
const num = (i:number) => String(i+1).padStart(2,'0');
---
<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy">
<section class="site-shell legal-page"><header class="legal-head"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="legal-lead">OpenCoven is a local-first platform. Your agent conversations, memory files, API keys, and personal data processed by the local Coven runtime live on your machine — not on this landing site. This policy explains the limited data the public OpenCoven website can handle and how optional analytics are constrained.</p><p class="legal-stamp">Effective date: May 27, 2026 · Last updated: August 31, 2026</p><div class="legal-highlight"><strong>Short version:</strong> The OpenCoven landing site does not receive your local agent sessions, conversations, workspace files, or API keys. Analytics are disabled by default. If an operator explicitly enables the repository's bounded event mode, only allowlisted website interaction events and approved technical context may be sent; prompts, commands, filenames, repository names, paths, raw errors, session replay, heatmaps, and broad autocapture are excluded by the shipped contract.</div></header>
<div class="legal-layout"><aside class="legal-toc"><h2>What this covers</h2><p class="muted">The short version is above. This is the detail, section by section.</p><nav aria-label="Privacy policy sections">{sections.map(([id,label],i)=><a href={`#${id}`}><span class="index">{num(i)}</span>{label}</a>)}</nav></aside><div class="legal-panels">
<section class="legal-panel" id="who-we-are"><h2>Who We Are</h2><p>OpenCoven ("we", "us", "our") is an open-source project building infrastructure for persistent AI familiars. Our website is available at <a href="https://opencoven.ai">opencoven.ai</a>. Questions? Email us at <a href="mailto:hello@opencoven.ai">hello@opencoven.ai</a>.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="what-we-dont-collect"><h2>What We Don't Collect</h2><p>Because the Coven runtime is local-first, this public landing site does not receive:</p><ul><li>Your agent conversations or session transcripts</li><li>Your MEMORY.md, daily notes, or workspace files</li><li>Your API keys (OpenAI, Anthropic, GitHub, etc.)</li><li>Your tool outputs, file reads, shell commands, or command results</li><li>Local data processed by the Coven daemon merely because you visit this website</li></ul><p>The landing repository's analytics mode is <strong>off by default</strong>. The shipped analytics contract also forbids prompts, commands, filenames, repository names, paths, raw error contents, session replay, heatmaps, and broad autocapture from analytics payloads.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="what-we-do-collect"><h2>What We Do Collect</h2><div class="legal-tablewrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Data collection details"><table class="legal-table"><thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th><th>When / retention</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bounded website interaction events and approved technical context</td><td>Diagnose public-site usage and conversion only when the deployment explicitly enables <code>events</code> analytics mode</td><td>Not collected by the default configuration. An enabled deployment must document its analytics provider, region, sampling, and retention before treating that mode as production-approved.</td></tr><tr><td>Support or security messages you choose to send by email, GitHub, or another linked channel</td><td>Respond to and resolve your request</td><td>Handled through the channel you choose and retained as needed for the request, project history, security response, or applicable legal obligations</td></tr><tr><td>Ordinary web request metadata handled by the hosting provider</td><td>Serve, secure, and operate the website</td><td>Subject to the hosting provider's operational and privacy terms</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>This page does not claim that the current landing site operates a newsletter signup, waitlist database, user account system, or GitHub OAuth login because those collection paths are not part of the checked-in public landing implementation.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="cookies"><h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2><p>The current static landing experience does not require cookies for its core navigation, documentation links, product discovery, Quickstart, or theme selection. Theme preference is stored locally in your browser.</p><p>Analytics are disabled unless the deployment explicitly sets the repository's analytics mode to <code>events</code> and provides the required analytics configuration. In that mode, the OpenCoven wrapper accepts only a fixed event allowlist and bounded property schema; session replay, heatmaps, exception capture, automatic page-view/page-leave capture, and general autocapture are disabled by the shipped configuration.</p><p>Third-party destinations linked from this site may set their own cookies or collect data after you navigate to them. Their policies govern that activity.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="third-party"><h2>Third-Party Services</h2><p>The public website and linked project workflows use or may direct you to the following services:</p><ul><li><strong>Vercel</strong> — website hosting and server-side landing endpoints; subject to <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel's Privacy Policy</a></li><li><strong>GitHub</strong> — source code, issues, security advisories, releases, and downloads</li><li><strong>Discord</strong> — an optional community destination</li><li><strong>PostHog</strong> — supported only for the explicitly enabled, bounded <code>events</code> analytics mode. The default build does not load the analytics client.</li></ul><p>When you use OpenCoven locally with third-party AI providers, communications with those providers are governed by the configuration you choose and those providers' terms. Visiting this landing site does not give the site access to those local prompts or responses.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="how-we-use"><h2>How We Use Your Data</h2><ul><li>Operate, secure, and improve the OpenCoven website and documentation</li><li>Respond to support, security, or other messages you deliberately send</li><li>Measure approved website interactions only when bounded event analytics are explicitly enabled</li></ul><p>We do not sell your data. We do not share landing-site data with advertisers. We do not use landing-site analytics to train AI models.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="storage"><h2>Data Storage and Security</h2><p>Data deliberately sent to OpenCoven through support or security channels is handled through the service you use to send it. Website hosting and any explicitly enabled analytics are handled by their configured providers. We limit collection in the landing implementation rather than relying on broad collection followed by filtering.</p><p>If bounded analytics are enabled for a production deployment, the deployment record must state the provider, hosting region, sampling policy, and retention period before that mode is considered approved. The default configuration remains off.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="your-rights"><h2>Your Rights</h2><p>Depending on your location and the data involved, you may have rights to access, correction, deletion, portability, objection, or restriction. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:hello@opencoven.ai">hello@opencoven.ai</a>.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="children"><h2>Children's Privacy</h2><p>OpenCoven is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13 through the public landing site.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="changes"><h2>Changes to This Policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy when the website's actual data flows, providers, or legal obligations change. Material changes should be reviewed together with the repository's analytics and deployment contracts.</p></section>
<section class="legal-panel" id="contact"><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions, concerns, or requests? Email <a href="mailto:hello@opencoven.ai">hello@opencoven.ai</a>. For security vulnerabilities, use the private reporting path on the <a href="/security">Security page</a>.</p></section>
</div></div></section></SiteLayout>
